---
export const title = 'Saving';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  Saving a changed text fires a cancelable <code>change</code> with <code>detail.value</code>. An
  unchanged text just closes the editor. The app answers in one of three ways:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Synchronous:</b> do nothing. The component sets <code>value</code> and closes.</li>
  <li>
    <b>Rejected:</b> call <code>event.preventDefault()</code>. The editor stays open; set
    <code>error-text</code> to say why.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Asynchronous:</b> set <code>loading</code> in the handler. The editor stays open and read
    only with a progress indicator. When the server answers, set <code>loading</code> back to
    false, with <code>error-text</code> set to keep the editor open on an error, or empty to close
    it. Set <code>value</code> first to show the server's version of the text.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  While <code>loading</code>, <kbd>Escape</kbd> and blur do nothing. Clear
  <code>error-text</code> when the next save starts and on <code>cancel</code>. With
  <code>required</code> a blank text is not saved and the editor shows a message.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 480px;'>
    <wc-inline-edit
      id='inline-edit-async'
      label='Project name'
      value='Apollo'
    ></wc-inline-edit>
    <p style='margin: 0.5rem 0 0;'>The demo server takes a second and rejects names with "fail".</p>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    const asyncEdit = document.querySelector('#inline-edit-async');
    asyncEdit.addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      const next = event.detail.value;
      asyncEdit.errorText = '';
      asyncEdit.loading = true;
      setTimeout(function () {
        if (next.toLowerCase().includes('fail')) {
          asyncEdit.errorText = 'The server rejected this name';
        } else {
          myConsole.log('saved: ' + next);
        }
        asyncEdit.loading = false;
      }, 1200);
    });
    asyncEdit.addEventListener('cancel', function () {
      asyncEdit.errorText = '';
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
